----------------------------------FILE COMMANDS-------------------
mkdir                     ---creates a new directory
rm(file name)             --removes or deletes a file 
rm -r (filename)                                 --removes a directory recursively
rm -rp (filename)                                ---recursively removes files without any confirmation
cp [source file] [destination file]              --- copies file from one to another directory
cp -r [source_directory] [destination_directory] --- recursively copies files from one to another directory
mv [source_file] [destination_file]              --- moves file from one to another directory
touch [file_name]                                --- creates a new file in the directory
cat [filename]                                   --shows the data in the files
cat >> [filename]                                -- used to add data in the files
head [filename]                                 --shows the  starting 10 lines of the file
tail [filename]                                 -- shows the last 10 lines of the code
nano[filename]                                  ---opens or creates a file using nano text editor
gpg -c [filename]                              -- encrypt a file
gpg [filename].gpg                              -- decrypt a file
wc -w [filename]                                --- shows the number of words,lines and bytes in the file
ls | xargs wc                                   ---- lists the number of lines,words,characters,in a each file in a directory
diff [firstfile] [secondfile]                    ---compares both the files and thn displays the differences

----------NAVIGATION COMMANDS------------
ls                   --listing directory
ls -a               --lists all the files even the hidden ones
ls -l               --lists files in vertical format
pwd                 ---shows the directory which im currently in
cd                  --change directory
cd ~                -- change directory
cd ..               --moves to previous directory
cd -                --changes to the previous directory
dirs                --shows current directory stack

----------------FILE TRANSFER COMMANDS----------------------
wget [linkofthewebserver]               ---downloads the file from the web server
curl -0 [linkoftheserver]               ---transfers data from one server to another with various protocols



------------USER AND GROUP COMMANDS-----------------
id                                ---sees details about the active users
last                              --shows the last system logins
who                               --displays who is logged in the system
w                                 ---shows which users are logged in and there activity
finger [username]                 ---shows user information
sudo useradd [username]           ---creates a new user account
sudo adduser [username]           ---creates a new user account using the adduser command interface
sudo userdel [username]           ---deletes the user account
